  # Resolves timezone metadata for a single target.  Target selector rules: - Use exactly one selector family: &#x60;tz&#x60;, &#x60;ip&#x60;, &#x60;lat&#x60; + &#x60;lon&#x60;, &#x60;offset&#x60;, or &#x60;auto_tz&#x3D;true&#x60;. - Bulk is not supported on this route. - With no selector the route returns 400 MISSING_TARGET. - &#x60;offset&#x60; queries return a specialized payload with &#x60;timezone&#x3D;null&#x60; and &#x60;matching_zones&#x60; for the request-time offset match. Only geographic zones are listed; &#x60;UTC&#x60; and &#x60;Etc/*&#x60; are intentionally excluded (use &#x60;tz&#x3D;UTC&#x60; for UTC). - &#x60;tz&#x60; names resolve to their canonical zone (&#x60;Europe/Stockholm&#x60; returns &#x60;Europe/Berlin&#x60;). - An &#x60;ip&#x60; with no timezone mapping returns 404 NOT_FOUND.  Examples: - Single target: &#x60;/v1/timezone?tz&#x3D;America/New_York&#x60; - Offset match: &#x60;/v1/timezone?offset&#x3D;-04:00&#x60;
  # @param [Hash] opts the optional parameters
  # @option opts [String] :tz IANA timezone name, matched case-insensitively. Links and aliases resolve to their canonical zone, so the returned &#x60;timezone&#x60; can differ (&#x60;Europe/Stockholm&#x60; returns &#x60;Europe/Berlin&#x60;, &#x60;UTC&#x60; returns &#x60;Etc/UTC&#x60;). &#x60;Etc/GMT+5&#x60; is UTC-05:00 (POSIX sign). On bulk-capable routes, a comma-separated list enables bulk mode with at most 10 values (any comma, even a trailing one, returns an array); request URLs are limited to 8192 characters. On single-target routes a list is rejected as an invalid timezone.
  # @option opts [String] :ip IP address. On bulk-capable routes, a comma-separated list enables bulk mode with at most 10 values; request URLs are limited to 8192 characters.
  # @option opts [Float] :lat Latitude. Must be provided together with &#x60;lon&#x60;.
  # @option opts [Float] :lon Longitude. Must be provided together with &#x60;lat&#x60;.
  # @option opts [String] :offset Fixed UTC offset in &#x60;+HH:MM&#x60; or &#x60;-HH:MM&#x60; format only (&#x60;+0530&#x60; and &#x60;+5&#x60; are rejected); URL-encode &#x60;+&#x60; as &#x60;%2B&#x60;, since an unencoded &#x60;+&#x60; is read as a space. An offset target returns &#x60;timezone&#x3D;null&#x60;. On bulk-capable routes, a comma-separated list enables bulk mode with at most 10 values; request URLs are limited to 8192 characters.
  # @option opts [Boolean] :auto_tz Set to &#x60;true&#x60; to resolve using the caller IP from Cloudflare headers. Counts as a selector family, so it cannot be combined with &#x60;tz&#x60;, &#x60;ip&#x60;, &#x60;lat&#x60;/&#x60;lon&#x60; or &#x60;offset&#x60;. Not supported on &#x60;/v1/time/clock&#x60;. Enabled by &#x60;true&#x60;, &#x60;1&#x60; or &#x60;yes&#x60; (case-insensitive); any other value leaves it off without an error.
  # @option opts [Boolean] :sign Set to &#x60;true&#x60;, &#x60;1&#x60; or &#x60;yes&#x60; (case-insensitive) to ask the gateway to sign the final JSON response. Any other value, a bare &#x60;sign&#x60;, or repeated &#x60;sign&#x60; values leave the response unsigned. Every authenticated JSON response, including errors, then includes signing headers. Not supported on &#x60;/v1/time/clock&#x60;.
